From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: full-grab tap takes no modifier events

What: setFullGrab no longer includes kCGEventFlagsChanged in its event tap
mask (CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyDown) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyUp)).
Modifier changes (flagsChanged) now arrive exclusively through the standard
AppKit sendEvent path while OmacVM's window is key.

Why: An active filter event tap (kCGEventTapOptionDefault) whose callback
returns NULL deletes the event from the system stream (CGEventTapCallBack).
While the VM has the keyboard, handleTapEvent does that for modifier
changes too, so other apps' global monitors (NSEvent
addGlobalMonitorForEventsMatchingMask:handler:) never see them. WeChat
Input (WeType) registers such a monitor for flagsChanged and, read from its
binary (an inference, not a run-time trace), its lone Shift switch is
reached from there. In #357 a lone Shift tap did not switch Chinese and
English in the VM; with this mask, the tap still on, it does. keyDown and
keyUp stay captured as before.

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM-specific input tap behavior; refs #357).

Test: app/runtime/Tests/keys/test-tap-no-flags.sh (CI: mask from this patch;
the runtime build: also that setFullGrab in ui/cocoa.m uses it). Applies after
omacvm-cocoa-tap-no-ask.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -1970,7 +1970,7 @@
 {
     COCOA_DEBUG("QemuCocoaView: setFullGrab\n");
 
-    CGEventMask mask = CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyDown) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyUp) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventFlagsChanged);
+    CGEventMask mask = CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyDown) | CGEventMaskBit(kCGEventKeyUp);
     CGEventTapPlacement place = omacvm_keys_place();
     if (!omacvm_tap_allowed()) {
         warn_report("Could not create event tap, system key combos will not be captured.\n");
